// N10 checkpoint 2: a dense match over enum variants dispatches to the
// correct arm, and a match with no accepting arm raises MATCH_ERROR at run
// time.
//
// R1 fix (PR #115 round 1): an earlier version of this comment said the
// literal JUMP_TABLE "out of [minTag, minTag+count) range" fallthrough is NOT
// reachable from any program that compiles. That is false.
// checkEnumExhaustiveness only checks that the ARMS name every constructor
// of THEIR OWN enum (compiler.cpp:1553-1568); it does not constrain the
// SUBJECT expression to that same enum. A subject of an unrelated enum type
// flows into a table-eligible match just as freely, and its tag comes from a
// different, wider tag space — so the literal default label IS reachable.
// test/translation-probes/27_jump_table_default_cross_enum.lox proves it:
// two enums, A (2 variants) and B (3), a match that is table-eligible and
// exhaustive over A's own 2 tags, given a real B() value at run time. B's
// tag (2) is outside A's own [0, 2) range, and the literal tableswitch
// default — not the sparse compare-and-branch form this file's own second
// match below uses — is what raises MATCH_ERROR.
//
// A guard, though, defeats table eligibility (so this uses the sparse
// GET_TAG/CONSTANT/EQUAL form, not JUMP_TABLE) WITHOUT defeating
// checkEnumExhaustiveness, which only reads each arm's constructor NAME, not
// its guard: a match with one arm per constructor, every guard false at run
// time, compiles as "exhaustive" yet accepts nothing, and MATCH_ERROR is
// exactly the real, reachable in-language shape that produces.
//
// Kept at script scope, printing each match directly (not `return`ed out of
// a function): AbstractStackTest.RunsOverEveryProbeWithNoInconsistency
// checks every probe's own RETURN sites have exactly the return value as a
// genuine operand-stack temporary (test_backend_abstract_stack.cpp's own
// checkReturnHeightZero) — a check this file's own header comment already
// says does not hold program-wide once a match's result is `return`ed
// (bytecode-translation-problems.md, "RETURN can return a named local"),
// so a `return match ...;` shape belongs under examples/, the way
// examples/or_pattern_demo.lox already uses it, not under
// test/translation-probes/.
enum Status { A B C D E }

print match C() {
    case A => "a"
    case B => "b"
    case C => "c"
    case D => "d"
    case E => "e"
};

print match B() {
    case A if false => "a"
    case B if false => "b"
    case C if false => "c"
    case D if false => "d"
    case E if false => "e"
};
